menu "UWB TWR Configuration"

    choice UWB_TWR_BOARD
        prompt "Target host board"
        default UWB_TWR_BOARD_STAMPS3
        help
            Select which host board's pin definitions (boards/stamps3.h,
            boards/atoms3.h, or boards/stampfly.h, at the repo root)
            main.cpp uses to configure uwb::Qm33120.

        config UWB_TWR_BOARD_STAMPS3
            bool "M5StampS3A"

        config UWB_TWR_BOARD_ATOMS3
            bool "M5 AtomS3"

        config UWB_TWR_BOARD_STAMPFLY
            bool "StampFly (M5StampS3A on drone, rear 12P FPC)"
            help
                M5StampS3A 背面に予約されている 12P FPC (0.5mm) 経由で
                接続する構成。SPI 4線に加えて RST / IRQ / WAKEUP がすべて
                取れる (boards/stampfly.h)。電源も同じコネクタの VDD_3V3
                から取るので降圧回路は要らない。
                旧 GROVE 4線構成は廃案 (2026-08-22)。

    endchoice

    choice UWB_BOARD_ATOMS3_PINOUT
        prompt "AtomS3 pin layout"
        depends on UWB_TWR_BOARD_ATOMS3
        default UWB_BOARD_ATOMS3_PINOUT_A
        help
            Selects which of the two AtomS3 pin layouts boards/atoms3.h
            builds (docs/IRQ_POLICY.md). Layout A repurposes the Grove port
            (G1/G2) for RST/IRQ and wires a ToF sensor to the bottom header
            (G38/G39); recommended for the plain AtomS3, whose G38/G39 are
            shared with the onboard MPU6886 IMU. Layout B instead uses the
            bottom header (G38/G39) for RST/IRQ and plugs the ToF sensor
            straight into the Grove port; recommended for AtomS3R, whose
            G38/G39 have nothing else attached.

        config UWB_BOARD_ATOMS3_PINOUT_A
            bool "Layout A: RST/IRQ=Grove(G1/G2), ToF I2C=G38/G39 (hand-wired to bottom header)"

        config UWB_BOARD_ATOMS3_PINOUT_B
            bool "Layout B: RST/IRQ=G38/G39, ToF I2C=Grove(G1/G2) (plug-and-play)"

    endchoice

    choice UWB_TWR_ROLE
        prompt "Device role"
        default UWB_TWR_ROLE_TAG
        help
            TAG (initiator) starts one ranging exchange every 200ms and logs
            success rate / distance statistics. ANCHOR (responder) blocks in
            a loop responding to polls; RxTimeout (no poll received yet) is
            treated as normal and not logged. Flash one board as TAG and a
            second board as ANCHOR (same PAN ID / addresses / PHY, i.e. same
            defaults) to range between them.

        config UWB_TWR_ROLE_TAG
            bool "TAG (initiator)"

        config UWB_TWR_ROLE_ANCHOR
            bool "ANCHOR (responder)"

    endchoice

    choice UWB_TWR_METHOD
        prompt "Ranging method"
        default UWB_TWR_METHOD_SS
        help
            SS-TWR (single-sided, requestRange()/respondRange()): one
            Poll/Response exchange, distance computed on the TAG side.
            DS-TWR (double-sided, requestDSRange()/respondDSRange()):
            adds a Final exchange and a Result frame; distance is computed
            on the ANCHOR side and relayed back to the TAG. Both sides of a
            link must use the same method.

        config UWB_TWR_METHOD_SS
            bool "SS-TWR"

        config UWB_TWR_METHOD_DS
            bool "DS-TWR"

    endchoice

    config UWB_TWR_TAG_ADDR
        hex "TAG (initiator) short address"
        range 0x0000 0xFFFE
        default 0x0001
        help
            The TWR short address used by the TAG role (requestRange()/
            requestDSRange() as initiatorAddress; also the address this
            build's ANCHOR role expects Poll frames to come from).

            Do not use 0xFFFF - it is the broadcast address. TAG and
            ANCHOR must agree on both this value and UWB_TWR_ANCHOR_ADDR,
            or ranging will not succeed (a mismatch just looks like "no
            response", the log alone cannot tell you which side is wrong).

    config UWB_TWR_ANCHOR_ADDR
        hex "ANCHOR (responder) short address"
        range 0x0000 0xFFFE
        default 0x0002
        help
            The TWR short address used by the ANCHOR role (respondRange()/
            respondDSRange()); also the responderAddress this build's TAG
            role targets.

            Do not use 0xFFFF - it is the broadcast address. TAG and
            ANCHOR must agree on both this value and UWB_TWR_TAG_ADDR, or
            ranging will not succeed.

    config UWB_SPI_FAST_HZ
        int "SPI fast clock override [Hz] (0 = use boards/*.h default)"
        range 0 32000000
        default 0
        help
            Overrides cfg.spi_fast_hz after it has been populated from
            boards/*.h's BOARD_*_UWB_PORT_CONFIG. The default, 0, leaves
            it untouched - i.e. exactly the boards/*.h value (currently
            16 MHz), identical to the behaviour before this option
            existed.

            Useful for bisecting a Device ID that cannot be read, or that
            reads back intermittently corrupted, by lowering the SPI
            clock. The QM33120W/DW3720 SPI clock ceiling is 32 MHz.

    config UWB_TWR_DIAG_REINIT_FAILS
        int "Diagnostic: re-run the PHY config after N consecutive failures (0 = off)"
        range 0 10000
        default 0
        help
            Diagnostic aid for task R10 (docs/GETTING_STARTED.md:1380). The
            M5Stamp UWB Module is channel-9 only, and on channel 9 the PLL
            must be recalibrated whenever the die temperature moves by
            20 degC (user manual 10.4) - which this repo does not do yet.

            With a non-zero N, the TAG re-runs uwb::Qm33120::init() after N
            consecutive failed ranging attempts, and the ANCHOR after N
            consecutive poll-wait timeouts. init() re-runs dwt_configure(),
            and with it the PLL calibration, at the current die temperature.
            Each attempt is logged as DIAG_REINIT with the die temperature
            before and after.

            The default, 0, disables this entirely: the build behaves
            exactly as it did before this option existed. This is an
            experiment, not a fix - the real fix is task R10.

    config UWB_TWR_POLL_WAIT_MS
        int "ANCHOR poll-wait window [ms] (0 = RangeConfig default, 200)"
        range 0 5000
        default 0
        help
            How long the ANCHOR keeps its receiver armed inside one
            respondRange() call while waiting for a poll
            (RangeConfig::pollHostTimeoutMs).

            This must be comfortably LONGER than the tag's poll interval.
            The window reopens a few ms after the previous exchange ends, so
            the next poll arrives (interval - a few ms) into it; when the
            window equals the poll interval the remaining margin is only a
            few ms, and nothing pulls the phase back to the middle. Measured
            on hardware: window 200 ms with a 200 ms interval gave a 1%
            success rate, while the same window with a 137 ms interval let
            the anchor see 429 of 430 polls.

    config UWB_TWR_DIAG_POLL_WAIT_RETURN_ON_RX_ERROR
        bool "Diagnostic: ANCHOR poll wait returns on the first RX error (pre-2026-08-29 behaviour)"
        default n
        help
            Sets RangeConfig::pollWaitReturnOnRxError / DSRangeConfig::
            pollWaitReturnOnRxError = true. Before 2026-08-29 this was the
            only behaviour: the ANCHOR's Poll-wait loop (respondRange() /
            respondDSRange()) called dwt_forcetrxoff() and returned
            Error::RxError the first time it saw a non-timeout RX error
            (RXPHE/RXFCE/RXFSL, as opposed to RXFTO/RXPTO).

            This mattered because the Poll-wait window
            (UWB_TWR_POLL_WAIT_MS, default 200 ms) and the tag's poll
            period (UWB_TWR_RANGE_INTERVAL_MS, also default 200 ms) are
            both quantized to the 1 ms FreeRTOS tick. A window that
            returns on every RX error re-phases itself onto whichever
            frame it was looking at when it returned; once a Poll landed
            in the blind gap between "window closes" and "window reopens"
            it stayed there for the rest of the run - this was the DS-TWR-
            specific root cause behind DS-TWR measuring 0-23% while SS-TWR
            measured 99.95% under otherwise identical conditions
            (docs/HANDOFF.md §0-C(1)).

            The default (n, pollWaitReturnOnRxError = false) instead
            clears the RX-error status bits and re-arms the receiver
            immediately, letting the Poll wait keep listening until
            UWB_TWR_POLL_WAIT_MS itself elapses - the same structure as
            Qorvo's own ex_05b_ds_twr_resp / ex_06b_ss_twr_resp responder
            examples, neither of which returns on an RX error.

            Enable this (y) only to reproduce the pre-2026-08-29 behaviour
            for A/B comparison; it is not expected to help on real
            hardware.

    config UWB_TWR_RANGE_INTERVAL_MS
        int "TAG poll interval [ms]"
        range 20 5000
        default 200
        help
            How often the TAG role starts a ranging exchange. 200 ms is the
            original hard-coded value.

            It is configurable because the ANCHOR re-arms its receiver on
            every respondRange() call and waits up to pollHostTimeoutMs
            (200 ms by default) for a poll. Two processes with nearly the
            same period can beat against each other, which looks like long
            dead stretches interrupted by short bursts of perfect success -
            the pattern measured on real hardware. Setting an interval that
            is not commensurate with the anchor's window (e.g. 137) tests
            for that: if the success rate changes, the loss was scheduling,
            not radio.

    config UWB_TWR_RETRY_MAX
        int "TAG: extra immediate retries on failure within one ranging cycle (0 = off)"
        range 0 5
        default 0
        help
            N = the maximum number of extra immediate ranging attempts the
            TAG makes, within the SAME ranging cycle, after a failed
            exchange - the cycle period (UWB_TWR_RANGE_INTERVAL_MS) itself
            is unchanged. Applies to BOTH TAG loops: SS-TWR (one exchange =
            Poll -> Response) and DS-TWR (one exchange = Poll / Response /
            Final [/ Result]). One exchange takes about 5-8 ms (SS-TWR) or
            a bit more (DS-TWR, one extra round trip) while the TAG only
            starts a new cycle every UWB_TWR_RANGE_INTERVAL_MS (measured
            ~137 ms on hardware for SS-TWR), so a retry just uses part of
            the otherwise idle time inside the same cycle. The measured
            per-attempt failure rate is about 3.5% for SS-TWR, and failures
            are mostly isolated (independent from one attempt to the
            next), so retrying once or twice is expected to lift the
            per-cycle success rate to roughly 99.9%.

            Every attempt - the first try and any retries - still counts
            individually in SS_RANGE_STAT/DS_RANGE_STAT, SEQ64 (SS-TWR
            only), and the UWB_TWR_DIAG_REINIT_FAILS consecutive-failure
            counter (SS-TWR only), exactly as before this option existed,
            so tools/serial/twr_stats.py's per-attempt rate is unaffected.
            New per-CYCLE counters (one cycle = the first attempt plus any
            retries it triggered) are logged separately as
            SS_CYCLE_STAT/DS_CYCLE_STAT and CSEQ64.

            The default, 0, disables this entirely: the TAG makes exactly
            one attempt per cycle, identical to the behaviour before this
            option existed. The ANCHOR role is not affected - it simply
            responds to whichever Poll it receives, retry or not.
            N = 1回の測距サイクル内で、失敗した交換の後にTAGが追加で即座に
            再試行する最大回数。サイクル周期 (UWB_TWR_RANGE_INTERVAL_MS)
            自体は変えない。SS-TWR・DS-TWR 両方のTAGループに適用される: SS-TWR
            は1回の交換 = Poll -> Response、DS-TWR は1回の交換 = Poll /
            Response / Final [/ Result]。1回の交換は約5-8ms（SS-TWR）または
            それより少し長く（DS-TWRは往復が1回多い）かかる一方、TAGが新しい
            サイクルを始めるのは UWB_TWR_RANGE_INTERVAL_MS ごと（SS-TWRで実測
            約137ms）なので、再試行は同じサイクル内のもともと空いている時間を
            使うだけ。実測の1試行あたり失敗率はSS-TWRで約3.5%で、失敗はほぼ
            独立事象（前後の試行と無関係）なので、1〜2回の再試行でサイクル
            あたりの成功率は99.9%程度まで上がる見込み。

            各試行（1回目・再試行とも）は、このオプションが追加される前と
            全く同じように、個別にSS_RANGE_STAT/DS_RANGE_STAT、SEQ64
            （SS-TWRのみ）、UWB_TWR_DIAG_REINIT_FAILS の連続失敗カウンタ
            （SS-TWRのみ）へ計上され続けるので、tools/serial/twr_stats.py が
            出す試行あたりの成功率には影響しない。サイクル単位（1回目の試行と
            それに続く再試行をまとめて1サイクルとする）の新しい集計は、別途
            SS_CYCLE_STAT/DS_CYCLE_STAT と CSEQ64 としてログに出す。

            既定の0ではこの機能は完全に無効: TAGは1サイクルにつき厳密に1回
            だけ試行し、このオプションが追加される前と同じ挙動になる。
            ANCHOR側の挙動はこのオプションの影響を受けない（再試行かどうかに
            関わらず、受信したPollには常に応答する）。

    config UWB_TWR_RETRY_DELAY_MS
        int "TAG: delay before each immediate retry attempt [ms] (0 = retry at once)"
        range 0 100
        default 0
        help
            Adds a delay of this many ms before each retry attempt within a
            ranging cycle (only takes effect when UWB_TWR_RETRY_MAX > 0),
            applied in addition to the existing fixed ~2ms gap before a
            retry's Poll (both TAG loops already wait 2ms so the ANCHOR has
            time to re-arm its receiver after the previous failed exchange).
            The default, 0, adds nothing - identical to the behaviour before
            this option existed.

            Rationale (DS-TWR): when the TAG's Response wait times out
            (about 4-6ms after its Poll), the ANCHOR may still be inside its
            own Final-wait window - it already answered that Poll with a
            Response and is now listening for a Final for several more ms
            (docs/HANDOFF.md section 0-C). An immediate retry Poll can land
            in that window, while the ANCHOR is not listening for Polls at
            all, and is simply lost. Measured on the bench: the 2nd-attempt
            (1st retry) failure rate was 44%, versus 10% for the 1st
            attempt (DS-TWR, 850kbps). A delay here lets the ANCHOR's own
            Final-wait window expire and return to Poll-wait before the
            retry's Poll goes out.

            Applies to BOTH TAG loops (SS-TWR and DS-TWR), same as
            UWB_TWR_RETRY_MAX. Does not change the ranging cycle period
            (UWB_TWR_RANGE_INTERVAL_MS): as already documented on
            UWB_TWR_RETRY_MAX, a cycle that takes longer (because of retries
            and now this delay) just makes the next cycle start right after
            it finishes, not exactly one UWB_TWR_RANGE_INTERVAL_MS after the
            previous cycle started.
            TAG: サイクル内の各再試行の前に、この値[ms]だけ追加の遅延を
            入れる（UWB_TWR_RETRY_MAX > 0のときのみ効果を持つ）。両TAGループに
            既にある、再試行のPoll送信前の固定約2msの小休止（ANCHORが直前の
            失敗した交換の後に受信機を再アームする時間を確保するため）に
            加えて適用する。既定の0は何も追加しない（このオプションが
            追加される前と同じ挙動）。

            根拠 (DS-TWR): TAGのResponse待ちがタイムアウトする（Pollから
            約4〜6ms後）とき、ANCHORはまだ自身のFinal待ち窓の中にいることが
            ある - そのPollには既にResponseで応答済みで、さらに数ms
            Finalを待ち続けている（docs/HANDOFF.md §0-C）。即座の再試行Pollは
            その窓の間に飛んでいき、ANCHORがPollを全く聞いていない状態で
            失われる。実機測定: 2回目の試行（1回目の再試行）の失敗率は
            44%で、1回目の試行の10%（DS-TWR, 850kbps）より大幅に高かった。
            ここで遅延を入れることで、再試行のPollを送る前にANCHOR自身の
            Final待ち窓が終わってPoll待ちへ戻るのを待てる。

            SS-TWR・DS-TWR両方のTAGループに適用される（UWB_TWR_RETRY_MAXと
            同じ）。測距サイクルの周期（UWB_TWR_RANGE_INTERVAL_MS）自体は
            変えない: UWB_TWR_RETRY_MAXで既に説明した通り、（再試行とこの
            遅延により）時間がかかったサイクルは終わった直後に次のサイクルが
            始まるだけであり、前のサイクル開始からちょうど
            UWB_TWR_RANGE_INTERVAL_MS後になるとは限らない。

    config UWB_TWR_DIAG_LOG_EVERY_FAIL
        bool "Diagnostic: log every failed ranging attempt, not just every 10th (both TAG loops)"
        default n
        help
            When y, both TAG loops (SS-TWR and DS-TWR) log every failed
            attempt with the usual FAIL line (SS_RANGE_STAT / DS_RANGE_STAT
            last=FAIL), instead of only every TAG_LOG_INTERVAL-th attempt
            (main.cpp, currently a hard-coded 10 - not itself a Kconfig
            option). In the DS-TWR loop this supersedes (is strictly wider
            than) the existing "log every failure whose stage is not
            ResponseWait" rule (2026-08-29 DS-TWR原因特定) - those still log
            too, plus now the ResponseWait-stage ones as well.

            Also adds an attempt=%u field to the FAIL line in both loops
            (0 = the cycle's first attempt, 1.. = retries, i.e. the same
            attempt counter used by the UWB_TWR_RETRY_MAX/
            UWB_TWR_RETRY_DELAY_MS per-cycle retry loop), so a retry's
            failure can be told apart from a first attempt's in the log
            regardless of this option's setting.

            The default, n, leaves both loops' FAIL logging exactly as it
            was before this option existed (periodic-only for SS-TWR,
            periodic + non-ResponseWait-stage for DS-TWR) - only the new
            attempt= field is always added.

            Verbose; intended for a retry-tuning counter-test (bench-only,
            alongside UWB_TWR_RETRY_MAX/UWB_TWR_RETRY_DELAY_MS), not routine
            use.
            診断用: y にすると、両TAGループ（SS-TWR・DS-TWR）が
            TAG_LOG_INTERVAL回（main.cppのハードコード値、現在10。Kconfig
            オプションではない）に1回の間引きではなく、失敗した試行を毎回
            ログに出す（通常のFAIL行: SS_RANGE_STAT / DS_RANGE_STAT
            last=FAIL）。DS-TWRループでは、既存の「stageがResponseWait以外の
            失敗は毎回ログ」ルール（2026-08-29 DS-TWR原因特定）を包含して
            広げる形になる（そちらも引き続きログされ、これに加えて
            ResponseWait段階の失敗も出るようになる）。

            両ループのFAIL行に attempt=%u フィールドも追加する（0=サイクルの
            最初の試行、1..=再試行。UWB_TWR_RETRY_MAX/UWB_TWR_RETRY_DELAY_MS
            のサイクル内再試行ループが使うのと同じ試行カウンタ）。これは
            このオプションの設定に関わらず常に追加され、再試行の失敗か
            最初の試行の失敗かをログだけで区別できるようにする。

            既定のnは、このオプションが追加される前と全く同じFAILログの
            挙動を保つ（SS-TWRは間引きのみ、DS-TWRは間引き+非ResponseWait
            段階のみ）- 新しい attempt= フィールドだけは常に追加される。

            冗長なため、再試行チューニングの切り分けテスト用
            （UWB_TWR_RETRY_MAX/UWB_TWR_RETRY_DELAY_MSと合わせてベンチでのみ
            使用）を想定しており、常用は想定していない。

    config UWB_TWR_DIAG_NO_LNA_PA
        bool "Diagnostic: do not enable external LNA/PA mode"
        default n
        help
            Sets PhyConfig::enableLnaPa = false, so dwt_setlnapamode(
            DWT_LNA_ENABLE | DWT_PA_ENABLE) is never called. That call
            repurposes DW3720 GPIOs to drive an external RF front end.

            Whether the M5Stamp UWB Module has such a front end, and whether
            M5Stack's own wrapper enables this mode, are both unverified in
            this checkout (no datasheet under docs/refs, no third_party/
            M5Stamp-UWB). This option makes it testable: it is a local RF
            setting, not an on-air parameter, so one side can be changed
            independently of the other.

    config UWB_TWR_DIAG_ROBUST_PHY
        bool "Diagnostic: most robust PHY (preamble 1024, PAC32, 850kbps)"
        default n
        help
            Replaces the default PHY settings (preamble 128 / PAC8 /
            6.8 Mbps) with the most robust combination the chip offers:
            preamble 1024 symbols, PAC 32, 850 kbps. This costs update rate
            and airtime but gives preamble detection far more margin.

            Use it to tell a marginal radio link apart from a timing or
            addressing problem: if the success rate jumps, the link was the
            limit. BOTH boards of a link must be flashed with the same
            setting - a one-sided change simply stops ranging.

            sfdTimeout is left at 0 so it is recomputed for the new preamble
            length (task R8): a fixed sfdTimeout silently destroys the
            reception rate when the preamble length changes.

    config UWB_TWR_DIAG_PHY_PREAMBLE
        int "Diagnostic: preamble length override (0 = leave the default 128)"
        default 0
        help
            Isolates the preamble-length half of UWB_TWR_DIAG_ROBUST_PHY so it
            can be measured on its own. 0 leaves PhyConfig at its default
            (128 / PAC8) untouched. 128, 256, 512 or 1024 sets that preamble
            length together with the PAC size Qorvo recommends for it
            (128->PAC8, 256->PAC16, 512->PAC16, 1024->PAC32).
            診断用: UWB_TWR_DIAG_ROBUST_PHY のうちプリアンブル長だけを取り出して
            単独で測れるようにする。0 なら PhyConfig の既定（128 / PAC8）の
            まま。128 / 256 / 512 / 1024 のいずれかを指定すると、その長さと
            Qorvo 推奨の PAC 長が一緒に設定される（128->PAC8、256->PAC16、
            512->PAC16、1024->PAC32）。

            BOTH boards must be flashed with the same value - a one-sided
            change simply stops ranging.
            両機を同じ値にすること。片側だけ変えると受信できない。

            sfdTimeout is left at 0, so it is recomputed from
            preambleLength/sfdType/pacSize (task R8): a fixed value silently
            destroys the reception rate when the preamble length changes.
            sfdTimeout は 0 のままにするので、preambleLength/sfdType/pacSize
            から自動計算される（課題 R8。固定値だと preamble を変えたときに
            受信率が黙って激減する）。

            When combined with UWB_TWR_DIAG_ROBUST_PHY, this option is applied
            afterwards and wins.
            UWB_TWR_DIAG_ROBUST_PHY と併用した場合は、こちらが後から上書きする。

    config UWB_TWR_DIAG_PHY_850K
        bool "Diagnostic: use 850 kbps instead of 6.8 Mbps"
        default n
        help
            Isolates the data-rate half of UWB_TWR_DIAG_ROBUST_PHY so it can
            be measured on its own: drops the data rate to 850 kbps only,
            leaving the preamble length unchanged.
            診断用: UWB_TWR_DIAG_ROBUST_PHY のうちデータ速度だけを取り出して
            単独で測れるようにする。データ速度だけを 850kbps へ落とし、
            プリアンブル長は変えない。

            BOTH boards must be flashed with the same value - a one-sided
            change simply stops ranging.
            両機を同じ値にすること。片側だけ変えると受信できない。

            When combined with UWB_TWR_DIAG_ROBUST_PHY, this option is applied
            afterwards and wins.
            UWB_TWR_DIAG_ROBUST_PHY と併用した場合は、こちらが後から上書きする。

    config UWB_TWR_DIAG_TXPOWER
        hex "Diagnostic: TX_POWER register override (0xfefefefe = ch9 default)"
        range 0x00000000 0xffffffff
        default 0xfefefefe
        help
            Overrides PhyConfig::txPower, which is written verbatim to the
            DW3720 TX_POWER register (4 bytes = 4 frame parts: TX_CP_PWR
            (STS)/TX_SHR_PWR/TX_PHR_PWR/TX_DATA_PWR, most-significant byte
            first - deca_device_api.h dwt_txconfig_t/dwt_settxpower comments).
            Within each byte, bits[7:2] are a 6-bit fine gain and bits[1:0]
            are a 2-bit coarse gain (dw3720_deca_regs.h TX_POWER_FINE_BIT_*/
            TX_POWER_COARSE_BIT_*); both count up toward more power (the
            per-step gain tables in dw3720_device.c are all positive), so a
            lower byte value means less transmit power. The default,
            0xfefefefe, is the Qorvo reference-design ch9 maximum (coarse=2,
            fine=63/63 in every byte - only one coarse step below the
            absolute ceiling 0xff).

            This is a diagnostic for the "PA overdrive / pulse distortion"
            hypothesis: SS-TWR failures on this hardware are almost all
            RXFSL (Reed-Solomon decode failure of the data part) and do not
            fall off with distance/received power, which is what an
            overdriven power amplifier distorting the pulses would look
            like regardless of range. Lowering this value tests that by
            simply reducing transmit power; if the failure rate drops, the
            hypothesis gains support.

            BOTH boards of a link must use the same value - a one-sided
            change makes the link asymmetric, not a fair A/B test.
            診断用: PhyConfig::txPower を上書きする。DW3720 の TX_POWER
            レジスタへそのまま書き込まれる4バイト値で、各バイトが送信
            フレームの4つの部分（上位から順に TX_CP_PWR(STS)/TX_SHR_PWR/
            TX_PHR_PWR/TX_DATA_PWR）に対応する。各バイト内は上位6bitが
            微調整ゲイン、下位2bitが粗調整ゲインで、どちらも値が大きい
            ほど送信電力が高い（dw3720_device.c のゲイン表はすべて正の
            増分）。既定値 0xfefefefe は Qorvo リファレンス設計の ch9 用
            最大値（各バイトとも粗=2・微=63/63で、絶対上限0xffより
            粗調整1段だけ低い）。

            SS-TWR の失敗はほぼ全て RXFSL（データ部のリードソロモン復号
            失敗）で、受信電力・距離が下がっても悪化しない（実測）。これは
            パワーアンプの過駆動でパルスが歪んでいる場合の見え方と一致する
            という仮説の検証用: 送信電力を下げて失敗率が下がれば仮説を
            支持する材料になる。

            両機を同じ値にすること。片側だけ変えるとA/B比較が成立しない。

    config UWB_TWR_DIAG_PGDELAY
        hex "Diagnostic: TX pulse-generator delay override (PGdly, 0x34 = ch9 default)"
        range 0x00 0x3F
        default 0x34
        help
            Overrides PhyConfig::pgDelay, which is written to the DW3720
            TX_CTRL_HI PG_DELAY bitfield via dwt_configuretxrf()
            (components/uwb_qm33120/src/uwb_qm33120.cpp toDwtTxConfig(),
            ~line 296). This is the TX pulse-generator delay, which sets the
            transmit pulse bandwidth. 0x34 is Qorvo's reference-design
            default for channel 9.

            Qorvo's API guide notes that the default TX config (PGdly
            0x34, power 0xfefefefe for ch9) suits Qorvo's own evaluation
            boards, and "for other hardware designs the values may need to
            be changed as part of the transmit power calibration activity."
            The M5Stamp UWB module has no board-level calibration, so this
            is a diagnostic sweep of PGdly to see whether ranging success
            changes with it.

            BOTH boards of a link must use the same value - a one-sided
            change makes the link asymmetric, not a fair A/B test. This is
            part of the per-board TX calibration that the M5Stamp module
            lacks.
            診断用: PhyConfig::pgDelay を上書きする。DW3720 の TX_CTRL_HI
            レジスタの PG_DELAY ビットフィールドへ dwt_configuretxrf() 経由
            で書き込まれる値（components/uwb_qm33120/src/uwb_qm33120.cpp の
            toDwtTxConfig()、296行目付近）。これは送信パルス発生器の遅延で、
            送信パルスの帯域幅を決める。0x34 は Qorvo リファレンス設計の
            ch9 用既定値。

            Qorvo の API ガイドには、既定の送信設定（ch9用 PGdly 0x34、
            power 0xfefefefe）は Qorvo 自身の評価ボード向けであり、「他の
            ハードウェア設計では、送信電力校正作業の一環としてこれらの値を
            変更する必要があるかもしれない」との記載がある。M5Stamp UWB
            モジュールには基板単位の校正がないため、PGdly を振って測距成功率
            が変化するかを確認する診断用オプション。

            両機を同じ値にすること。片側だけ変えるとA/B比較が成立しない。
            M5Stamp モジュールに欠けている基板単位の送信校正の一部。

    config UWB_TWR_DIAG_SFD_TYPE
        int "Diagnostic: SFD type override (4 = leave the default DW8; 0=IEEE4A 1=DW8 2=DW16 3=IEEE4Z)"
        range 0 4
        default 4
        help
            Overrides PhyConfig::sfdType, the Start-of-Frame-Delimiter
            sequence used for preamble/frame detection (enum class SfdType,
            components/uwb_qm33120/include/uwb_qm33120_types.hpp). 0=IEEE4A,
            1=DW8 (PhyConfig's own default), 2=DW16, 3=IEEE4Z. The default
            of this option, 4, leaves phy.sfdType untouched - i.e. exactly
            the behaviour before this option existed.

            Applied to both TAG and ANCHOR builds: main.cpp builds one
            shared uwb::PhyConfig before begin(), regardless of role.

            sfdTimeout is left at 0 (auto), so it keeps tracking the
            automatic calculation for whichever SFD length the selected type
            uses (sfdSymbols() in components/uwb_qm33120/src/uwb_qm33120.cpp:
            IEEE4A/DW8/IEEE4Z = 8 symbols, DW16 = 16 symbols) - a fixed
            sfdTimeout would silently destroy the reception rate when the
            SFD length changes (the same pitfall as UWB_TWR_DIAG_PHY_PREAMBLE
            / task R8 for preamble length).

            BOTH boards of a link must use the same value - a one-sided
            change simply stops ranging.
            診断用: PhyConfig::sfdType（プリアンブル/フレーム検出に使う
            SFD（フレーム開始区切り）シーケンス。enum class SfdType、
            components/uwb_qm33120/include/uwb_qm33120_types.hpp）を
            上書きする。0=IEEE4A、1=DW8（PhyConfig 自体の既定）、2=DW16、
            3=IEEE4Z。このオプションの既定値4は phy.sfdType に触れない
            （このオプションが追加される前と完全に同じ挙動）。

            TAG・ANCHOR両方のビルドに適用される（main.cpp はロールによらず
            begin() の前に共通の uwb::PhyConfig を1つ組み立てる）。

            sfdTimeout は 0（自動計算）のままにするので、選んだ種別の SFD 長
            （components/uwb_qm33120/src/uwb_qm33120.cpp の sfdSymbols():
            IEEE4A/DW8/IEEE4Z=8シンボル、DW16=16シンボル）に応じた自動計算に
            追随し続ける。固定値のままだと SFD 長を変えたときに受信率が黙って
            激減する（UWB_TWR_DIAG_PHY_PREAMBLE・課題R8のプリアンブル長と同じ
            罠）。

            両機を同じ値にすること。片側だけ変えると受信できなくなる。

    config UWB_TWR_DIAG_PREAMBLE_CODE
        int "Diagnostic: TX/RX preamble code override (0 = leave the default 9/9; ch9/64MHz PRF codes are 9-12)"
        range 0 12
        default 0
        help
            Overrides both PhyConfig::txPreambleCode and
            PhyConfig::rxPreambleCode (default 9 each) to the given value in
            one shot. On channel 9 (64 MHz PRF - the only channel this module
            supports, see uwb-module-ch9-only), the valid preamble codes are
            9-12 (IEEE 802.15.4z). The default of this option, 0, leaves both
            fields untouched - i.e. exactly the default behaviour (9/9).

            Applied to both TAG and ANCHOR builds - same shared PhyConfig
            code path as UWB_TWR_DIAG_SFD_TYPE above.

            BOTH boards of a link must use the same value - a one-sided
            change simply stops ranging (the TX and RX preamble code must
            match on both ends for correlator lock).
            診断用: PhyConfig::txPreambleCode と rxPreambleCode（既定はいずれも
            9）を、指定した値へまとめて上書きする。ch9（64MHz PRF。本モジュール
            が対応する唯一のチャネル）で有効なプリアンブルコードは9〜12
            （IEEE 802.15.4z）。このオプションの既定値0は両方のフィールドに
            触れない（既定の 9/9 のまま）。

            TAG・ANCHOR両方のビルドに適用される（UWB_TWR_DIAG_SFD_TYPE と同じ
            共通 PhyConfig 経路）。

            両機を同じ値にすること。片側だけ変えると受信できなくなる
            （相関器のロックには送受両端でプリアンブルコードが一致している
            必要がある）。

    config UWB_TWR_DIAG_RESP_TX_DELAY_UUS
        int "Diagnostic: SS-TWR response TX delay override [UUS] (0 = leave the timing-profile value)"
        range 0 20000
        default 0
        help
            Overrides RangeConfig::responseTxDelayUus in the SS-TWR
            (single-sided) makeRangeConfig() of BOTH the TAG and the ANCHOR
            role, applied AFTER uwb::applyTimingProfile() so it wins over
            whichever UWB_TIMING_PROFILE preset ended up effective at
            runtime (docs/TIMING_PRESETS.md; init() can downgrade an IRQ
            preset to PollingBoth if the IRQ line turns out dead). The
            default of this option, 0, leaves responseTxDelayUus untouched -
            i.e. exactly the timing-profile's value, identical to the
            behaviour before this option existed. DS-TWR's makeRangeConfig()
            is not touched by this option.

            The receive window is grown to match, so a longer response delay
            does not by itself cause a receive timeout:
              rxTimeoutUus = (profile-effective rxTimeoutUus)
                             + (this value - RESPONSE_TX_DLY_UUS)
            i.e. the receive window that applyTimingProfile() has already
            set (PollingBoth: 4500 UUS) grows by the same delta; it is never
            shrunk (a delta <= 0 leaves the window untouched).

            BOTH boards of a link must use the same value - a one-sided
            change breaks the deadline inequality
            (docs/TIMING_PRESETS.md section 1.2) on one side only.
            診断用: SS-TWR（片側測距）の makeRangeConfig()（TAG・ANCHOR両方）で
            RangeConfig::responseTxDelayUus を上書きする。
            uwb::applyTimingProfile() の**後**に適用するので、実行時に実際に
            有効な UWB_TIMING_PROFILE プリセット（docs/TIMING_PRESETS.md。
            IRQ 線が死んでいると init() が IRQ プリセットを PollingBoth へ
            降格させることがある）が何であっても、こちらが最終的に勝つ。
            このオプションの既定値0は responseTxDelayUus に触れない
            （プリセットの値のまま、このオプションが追加される前と完全に
            同じ挙動）。DS-TWR の makeRangeConfig() はこのオプションで変更
            しない。

            受信待ち窓もあわせて広げる（応答遅延だけ伸ばすと受信タイムアウト
            の原因になりうるため）:
              rxTimeoutUus = (プロファイル適用後の実効 rxTimeoutUus)
                             + (この値 - RESPONSE_TX_DLY_UUS)
            すなわち applyTimingProfile() が設定済みの受信窓（PollingBoth
            では 4500 UUS）に同じ延長分を足す。縮めることはしない
            （差が 0 以下なら窓は変更しない）。

    config UWB_TWR_DIAG_FINAL_TX_DELAY_UUS
        int "Diagnostic: DS tag Final delayed-TX offset override [UUS] (0 = preset default)"
        range 0 20000
        default 0
        help
            Overrides DSRangeConfig::finalTxDelayUus in the DS-TWR TAG's
            makeRangeConfig(), applied AFTER uwb::applyTimingProfile() so it
            wins over whichever UWB_TIMING_PROFILE preset ended up effective
            at runtime (docs/TIMING_PRESETS.md; init() can downgrade an IRQ
            preset to PollingBoth if the IRQ line turns out dead). The
            default of this option, 0, leaves finalTxDelayUus untouched -
            i.e. exactly the firmware's built-in value (currently 3000).
            Applies to the DS TAG only; the DS ANCHOR's makeRangeConfig() is
            not touched by this option.

            Used to reproduce the DW3000 UM section 9.4.1 delayed-TX errata:
            the old preset value 1800 at 850kbps/preamble256 left only
            0.04-1.04ms of margin before the deadline, which is why it was
            raised to the new preset of 3000 (docs/HANDOFF.md section 0-C).
            This option lets a test build dial finalTxDelayUus back down (or
            further up) without editing code, to reproduce or bracket that
            errata on the bench.

            CORRECTED 2026-08-30 (measured on the bench, build e30): the
            claim that used to be here - "any override value >= 1500 is
            still inside the ANCHOR's window and will be received" - is
            WRONG. The two fields are measured from different reference
            points: this option (TAG side) counts from the Response frame's
            RMARKER, while the ANCHOR's
            UWB_TWR_DIAG_FINAL_RX_AFTER_RESP_TX_DELAY_UUS counts from the
            ANCHOR's own Response TX completion (dwt_setrxaftertxdelay()) -
            offset by the Response frame's remaining on-air time after its
            RMARKER (~267us at 850kbps/preamble256/24-byte Response;
            docs/TIMING_PRESETS.md section 2.4, docs/HANDOFF.md section
            0-C). Concretely, at 850kbps/preamble256 the TAG's Final
            preamble starts at (this option's value, in real us) - 264 UUS
            (~270us, the SHR length) after the Response RMARKER. With this
            option set to 1800 and the ANCHOR left at its default 1500, the
            ANCHOR's RX window opens ~228us AFTER the Final preamble has
            already started (only ~41us of SHR left when it opens), so the
            Final is missed 100% of the time (measured 2026-08-30, e30:
            0/690). To actually test 1800 on the bench, also set the
            ANCHOR's UWB_TWR_DIAG_FINAL_RX_AFTER_RESP_TX_DELAY_UUS=500 (the
            pre-2026-08-29 anchor value), which opens the window well before
            the Final preamble arrives.
            診断用: DS-TWR TAG の makeRangeConfig() で
            DSRangeConfig::finalTxDelayUus を上書きする。
            uwb::applyTimingProfile() の**後**に適用するので、実行時に実際に
            有効な UWB_TIMING_PROFILE プリセット（docs/TIMING_PRESETS.md。
            IRQ 線が死んでいると init() が IRQ プリセットを PollingBoth へ
            降格させることがある）が何であっても、こちらが最終的に勝つ。
            このオプションの既定値0は finalTxDelayUus に触れない
            （ファームウェア組み込みの現在値3000のまま）。DS TAG限定で、
            DS ANCHOR の makeRangeConfig() はこのオプションで変更しない。

            DW3000 UM §9.4.1の遅延送信エラッタを机上再現するためのもの:
            旧プリセット値1800（850kbps/preamble256）では締切までの余裕が
            0.04〜1.04msしかなく、これが新プリセット3000への引き上げ理由
            だった（docs/HANDOFF.md §0-C）。このオプションでコード修正なしに
            finalTxDelayUusを下げ（あるいはさらに上げ）て、実機でこの
            エラッタを再現・境界確認できる。

            【2026-08-30訂正、実機e30で確認】ここに以前あった「上書き値が
            1500以上であれば窓の内側に収まり受信される」という記述は誤り
            だった。2つの値は基準点が異なる: 本オプション（TAG側）は
            ResponseフレームのRMARKER基準、ANCHOR側の
            UWB_TWR_DIAG_FINAL_RX_AFTER_RESP_TX_DELAY_UUSは自分の
            Response送信完了（dwt_setrxaftertxdelay()）基準で、両者は
            ResponseのRMARKER後の残り伝送時間（850kbps/preamble256/
            24バイトのResponseで≈267µs。docs/TIMING_PRESETS.md §2.4、
            docs/HANDOFF.md §0-C参照）だけずれる。具体的には850kbps/
            preamble256でタグのFinalプリアンブル先頭は、本オプションの値
            （実µs換算）−264 UUS（≈270µs、SHR長）だけResponseのRMARKER後に
            来る。本オプションを1800、ANCHOR側を既定の1500のままにすると、
            ANCHORの受信窓はFinalのプリアンブルが始まった**後**（≈228µs
            遅れて）開き、開いた時点で残るSHRはわずか≈41µsしかないため
            Finalを100%取りこぼす（2026-08-30実測、e30: 0/690）。実機で
            1800を試す場合は、ANCHOR側の
            UWB_TWR_DIAG_FINAL_RX_AFTER_RESP_TX_DELAY_UUS=500（2026-08-29
            より前のANCHOR既定値）も同時に設定すること。この値なら窓は
            Finalプリアンブル到達より十分前に開く。

    config UWB_TWR_DIAG_FINAL_RX_AFTER_RESP_TX_DELAY_UUS
        int "Diagnostic: DS anchor Final RX-after-Response-TX delay override [UUS] (0 = preset default)"
        range 0 20000
        default 0
        help
            Overrides DSRangeConfig::finalRxAfterResponseTxDelayUus in the
            DS-TWR ANCHOR's makeRangeConfig(), applied AFTER
            uwb::applyTimingProfile() so it wins over whichever
            UWB_TIMING_PROFILE preset ended up effective at runtime
            (docs/TIMING_PRESETS.md; init() can downgrade an IRQ preset to
            PollingBoth if the IRQ line turns out dead). The default of this
            option, 0, leaves finalRxAfterResponseTxDelayUus untouched -
            i.e. exactly the firmware's built-in value (currently 1500).
            Applies to the DS ANCHOR only; the DS TAG's makeRangeConfig() is
            not touched by this option.

            Used to rebuild the pre-fix timing for a counter-test: the value
            was 500 before 2026-08-29 (docs/HANDOFF.md section 0-C), raised
            to 1500 in the same fix that raised the TAG's
            UWB_TWR_DIAG_FINAL_TX_DELAY_UUS preset from 1800 to 3000, so the
            two stayed symmetric - finalTxDelayUus (TAG) and
            finalRxAfterResponseTxDelayUus (ANCHOR) both describe the same
            physical gap (the Final frame's flight time after the Response)
            from opposite ends of the link.
            診断用: DS-TWR ANCHOR の makeRangeConfig() で
            DSRangeConfig::finalRxAfterResponseTxDelayUus を上書きする。
            uwb::applyTimingProfile() の**後**に適用するので、実行時に実際に
            有効な UWB_TIMING_PROFILE プリセット（docs/TIMING_PRESETS.md。
            IRQ 線が死んでいると init() が IRQ プリセットを PollingBoth へ
            降格させることがある）が何であっても、こちらが最終的に勝つ。
            このオプションの既定値0は finalRxAfterResponseTxDelayUus に
            触れない（ファームウェア組み込みの現在値1500のまま）。DS
            ANCHOR限定で、DS TAG の makeRangeConfig() はこのオプションで
            変更しない。

            机上再現用の切り分けテストのためのもの: 2026-08-29
            (docs/HANDOFF.md §0-C) より前の値は500で、TAG側の
            UWB_TWR_DIAG_FINAL_TX_DELAY_UUS のプリセットを1800から3000へ
            引き上げたのと同じ修正で1500へ引き上げ、両者を対称に保った
            （finalTxDelayUus（TAG側）と finalRxAfterResponseTxDelayUus
            （ANCHOR側）は、リンクの両端から見た同じ物理的な間隔
            ―Responseの後にFinalフレームが飛んでいる時間―を指す）。

    config UWB_TWR_DIAG_DS_HOST_TIMEOUT_MS
        int "Diagnostic: DS-TWR hostTimeoutMs override [ms], both TAG and ANCHOR (0 = preset default)"
        range 0 1000
        default 0
        help
            Overrides DSRangeConfig::hostTimeoutMs in BOTH the DS-TWR TAG's
            and the DS-TWR ANCHOR's makeRangeConfig(), applied AFTER
            uwb::applyTimingProfile() so it wins over whichever
            UWB_TIMING_PROFILE preset ended up effective at runtime. The
            default of this option, 0, leaves hostTimeoutMs untouched - i.e.
            exactly the firmware's built-in value (currently 20). Unlike the
            other DS diagnostics above, this one option applies to both
            roles' makeRangeConfig() at once, because hostTimeoutMs is the
            same host-side polling backstop on both ends: requestDSRange()
            (TAG - waits for Response/Final/Result) and respondDSRange()'s
            Final-wait loop (ANCHOR) both use it (the separate Poll-wait
            uses pollHostTimeoutMs, untouched by this option).

            Used to rebuild the pre-fix timing for a counter-test: the value
            was 10ms before 2026-08-29 (docs/HANDOFF.md section 0-C), raised
            to 20ms because the margin against the hardware RX-frame-timeout
            (RXFTO) that actually closes the Final RX window was only
            about 2.5ms (RXFTO fires about 7.5ms after the Response
            delayed-TX is armed; a 10ms host timeout could race it if
            host-side logging or scheduling jitter shifted the host clock
            by more than that).
            診断用: DSRangeConfig::hostTimeoutMs を DS-TWR TAG・ANCHOR
            両方の makeRangeConfig() で上書きする。uwb::applyTimingProfile()
            の**後**に適用するので、実行時に有効な UWB_TIMING_PROFILE
            プリセットが何であってもこちらが勝つ。このオプションの既定値0は
            hostTimeoutMs に触れない（ファームウェア組み込みの現在値20の
            まま）。上の他のDS診断オプションと違い、これは1個のオプションで
            両ロールの makeRangeConfig() に同時に適用される。hostTimeoutMs
            は両端で同じ役割のホスト側ポーリング上限だからで、
            requestDSRange()（TAG側。Response/Final/結果フレームを待つ）と
            respondDSRange()のFinal待ちループ（ANCHOR側）の両方がこれを
            使う（Poll待ちは別フィールドpollHostTimeoutMsを使い、この
            オプションでは変更しない）。

            机上再現用の切り分けテストのためのもの: 2026-08-29
            (docs/HANDOFF.md §0-C) より前の値は10msで、Final受信窓を
            実際に閉じるハードウェアのRXFTO（受信フレームタイムアウト）に
            対する余裕が約2.5msしかなかった（Response遅延送信を予約して
            からRXFTOが立つまで約7.5ms。ホスト側のログ出力等でジッタが
            それを超えると逆転しうる）ため、20msへ引き上げた。

    config UWB_TWR_DIAG_RF_PORT
        int "Diagnostic: RF port control (0=driver default, 1=force RF1, 2=force RF2, 3=auto 1->2, 4=auto 2->1)"
        range 0 4
        default 0
        help
            Calls dwt_configure_rf_port() after begin() with the given
            dwt_rf_port_ctrl_e value. The QM33120W has RF1 (TX/RX) and RF2
            (RX only, for PDoA); on the M5Stamp UWB module RF2 is terminated
            with 49.9 ohm, so only RF1 has an antenna. 0 leaves the driver
            default (automatic switching). Used to test whether the RX port
            selection contributes to per-frame random reception failures.
            begin() の後に dwt_configure_rf_port() を指定値で呼ぶ。QM33120W は
            RF1 (送受) と RF2 (受信専用、PDoA 用) を持ち、M5Stamp UWB モジュール
            では RF2 は 49.9 Ω で終端されアンテナは RF1 のみ。0 はドライバ既定
            (自動切替) のまま。受信ポート選択がフレームごとのランダムな受信
            失敗に寄与しているかを切り分けるための診断。

    config UWB_TWR_DIAG_PLL_COARSE_CH9
        int "Diagnostic: force ch9 PLL VCO coarse-tune code after init and re-lock (0 = off)"
        range 0 127
        default 0
        help
            Diagnostic for the "SS-TWR success rate is fixed at the TAG's
            init() time by die temperature" finding documented next to
            logCalibrationDump() in main.cpp: boots with die temp <=31degC
            get PLL_COARSE_CODE's ch9 VCO coarse-tune field (bits[6:0]) =
            0x23 (35, equal to the OTP-programmed value) and 38-65% SS-TWR
            success; boots at >=32degC get 0x24 (36) and 10-20% success.
            Hypothesis: 0x24 leaves the VCO on a sub-band edge, giving worse
            phase noise, and that is what fails 6.8 Mbps data decode.

            With a non-zero value N, right after the boot "cal:" dump the
            device forces the ch9 coarse-tune code to N and re-locks the PLL
            on it via a raw register sequence (PLL_COARSE_CODE + PLL_CAL's
            USE_OLD/TUNE_OVR bits, escalating through up to three variants
            A/B/C if the previous one's readback did not match - see
            diagForcePllCoarseCh9()'s doc comment in main.cpp for the exact
            register-level sequence and SDK evidence for each write). The
            SDK's own public entry point for this, dwt_pll_chx_auto_cal(),
            was tried first but returned 254 (not a documented status code)
            and left PLL_COARSE_CODE unchanged on real hardware - it never
            actually forced anything, hence the raw-register replacement.
            Each sequence's result (requested vs. readback code, PLL_CAL
            before/after, PLL_STATUS, lock flag, return code) is logged as
            DIAG_PLL_COARSE(A)/(B)/(C), followed by a final DIAG_PLL_COARSE
            summary line and another full logCalibrationDump().

            This does not fix the underlying temperature dependency (task
            R10) - it only tests, at whatever temperature this boot happened
            to be at, whether forcing the code the cold-boot case gets
            changes the SS-TWR success rate. Since which board(s) boot warm
            is not controlled, both TAG and ANCHOR read this same option;
            set it on whichever board(s) need it (harmless, if unnecessary,
            to also set it on a board that already got 0x23 on its own -
            the forced value simply matches what the hardware search already
            picked). The default, 0, disables this entirely: the build
            behaves exactly as it did before this option existed.
            診断用。main.cppのlogCalibrationDump()近くに記載した「SS-TWRの
            成功率はタグのinit()時点のダイ温度で決まる」という測定結果への
            切り分け: ダイ温度31度以下で起動すると、PLL_COARSE_CODEのch9
            VCO粗調整フィールド（bits[6:0]）が0x23（35、OTP書き込み値と
            一致）になり成功率38-65%、32度以上で起動すると0x24（36）に
            なり成功率10-20%になる（実測）。仮説: 0x24はVCOがサブバンドの
            境界に乗っており位相雑音が悪化し、それが6.8Mbpsのデータ部
            復号失敗を招いている、というもの。

            0以外の値Nを設定すると、起動時の"cal:"ダンプの直後に、ch9の
            粗調整コードをNへ強制し、生のレジスタ操作（PLL_COARSE_CODEと
            PLL_CALのUSE_OLD/TUNE_OVRビット）でPLLを再ロックする。前段の
            読み戻しが一致しなければ最大3段階A/B/Cへ段階的にエスカレート
            する（各書き込みの正確なレジスタ順序とSDK上の根拠は
            main.cppのdiagForcePllCoarseCh9()のドキュメントコメント
            参照）。任意の粗調整コードをロックするためのSDK公開API
            dwt_pll_chx_auto_cal()を最初に試したが、実機では254
            （文書化されたステータスコードではない）を返しPLL_COARSE_CODE
            は変化しなかった - 実際には何も強制していなかったため、生の
            レジスタ操作へ置き換えた。各シーケンスの結果（要求コード対
            読み戻しコード、前後のPLL_CAL、PLL_STATUS、ロックフラグ、
            戻り値）をDIAG_PLL_COARSE(A)/(B)/(C)としてログに出し、最後に
            DIAG_PLL_COARSEのまとめ行と、logCalibrationDumpをもう一度
            出す。

            温度依存性そのものの修正ではない（本命はタスクR10) -
            そのブートがたまたま何度だったかにかかわらず、コールドブート
            時のコードへ強制すると成功率が変わるかだけを見る診断。どちらの
            機体がウォームブートするかは制御できないため、TAGとANCHORの
            両方が同じオプションを読む。必要な機体だけに設定すればよい
            （既に自力で0x23を得ている機体に設定しても、強制値がハード
            ウェア探索の結果と一致するだけで無害）。既定の0ではこの機能は
            完全に無効 - このオプションが追加される前と同じ挙動になる。

    choice UWB_TWR_DIAG_RECAL_KIND
        prompt "Diagnostic: re-run one chip calibration once at runtime (NONE = off)"
        default UWB_TWR_DIAG_RECAL_NONE
        help
            Diagnostic for the "which one-shot init-time calibration makes
            the SS-TWR success rate depend on die temperature at init()"
            question documented next to logCalibrationDump() in main.cpp
            (cold boot ~30degC -> 47-65%, warm reboot ~37degC -> 10-25%,
            unchanged afterwards). With a choice other than NONE, the TAG
            re-runs the selected calibration exactly once,
            UWB_TWR_DIAG_RECAL_SEC seconds after boot, and re-dumps the
            "cal:" register lines (logCalibrationDump()) so the run can be
            compared against the boot-time dump from the same log. The
            success rate before/after can be read off the cumulative
            count/ok fields already logged in SS_RANGE_STAT, using the
            count=/ok= values the "RECAL(...)" log line reports at the
            moment it fires as the split point.

            The default, NONE, disables this entirely - the build behaves
            exactly as it did before this option existed.
            診断用: SS-TWR成功率がタグのinit()時点のダイ温度に依存する現象
            （main.cppのlogCalibrationDump()近くに記載。コールドブート約30度
            →47-65%、ウォームリブート約37度→10-25%、その後は変化しない）の
            原因が、init()内で一度だけ走るキャリブレーションのどれにあるかを
            切り分ける。NONE以外を選ぶと、起動からUWB_TWR_DIAG_RECAL_SEC秒後
            にタグが選択したキャリブレーションを1回だけやり直し、"cal:"
            レジスタダンプ（logCalibrationDump()）を出し直すので、同じログ
            内で起動時ダンプと比較できる。前後の成功率は、SS_RANGE_STATに
            既に出ている累積count/okのうち、"RECAL(...)" 行がその時点で
            報告するcount=/ok=を境目として読み取ればよい。

            既定のNONEでは何も起きない。このオプションが追加される前と
            完全に同一の挙動になる。

        config UWB_TWR_DIAG_RECAL_NONE
            bool "Off (no re-calibration)"

        config UWB_TWR_DIAG_RECAL_ADC
            bool "ADC offset: dwt_restoreconfig(DWT_RESTORE_TXRX_MODE | DWT_FORCE_ADCOFFSET_CAL)"
            help
                Forces the ADC offset calibration - the one calibration the
                SDK's own comment documents as temperature-dependent in this
                range (dw3720_device.c:1716-1718, "force ADC cal ... once
                when temperature >= 20C") - via
                dwt_restoreconfig(DWT_RESTORE_TXRX_MODE |
                DWT_FORCE_ADCOFFSET_CAL) (deca_device_api.h:1882). Along the
                way this also unconditionally re-runs the PGF cal, and
                restores the PLL only if PLL_STATUS_PLL_LOCK_FLAG is
                currently clear - so it does not force a PLL recalibration
                (dw3720_device.c:1656 ull_restoreconfig() -> :1730
                ull_restore_txrx() -> :1690 ull_restore_pll()).
                最も温度依存性が明記されているADCオフセット校正を強制する
                （dw3720_device.c:1716-1718: 「温度20度以上で1回ADC校正を
                強制」）。途中でPGF校正も無条件に走るが、PLLは現在ロックが
                外れているときだけ復元される（＝PLLの強制再校正ではない）。

        config UWB_TWR_DIAG_RECAL_PGF
            bool "PGF RX I/Q: dwt_pgf_cal(1)"
            help
                Re-runs only the receive pulse-generator filter (PGF) I/Q
                calibration, via dwt_pgf_cal(1) (deca_device_api.h:3301 ->
                dw3720_device.c:2133 ull_pgf_cal() -> :2172
                ull_run_pgfcal()).
                PGF校正（受信I/Q校正）だけをやり直す。

        config UWB_TWR_DIAG_RECAL_PLL
            bool "Hardware PLL: dwt_pll_cal()"
            help
                Re-runs only the hardware PLL calibration, via
                dwt_pll_cal() (deca_device_api.h:3326 ->
                dw3720_device.c:6683 ull_pll_cal(): forces IDLE_RC then
                IDLE, the latter re-triggering the same hardware PLL-cal
                state machine documented in main.cpp's logCalibrationDump()
                PLL comment).
                ハードウェアPLL校正だけをやり直す。

        config UWB_TWR_DIAG_RECAL_FULL
            bool "Full re-init: uwb::Qm33120::init() (same path as UWB_TWR_DIAG_REINIT_FAILS)"
            help
                Re-runs uwb::Qm33120::init() - the same call
                UWB_TWR_DIAG_REINIT_FAILS already uses (diagReinit() in
                main.cpp) - which redoes dwt_configure() and with it the
                PLL/PGF/ADC calibrations together, at the current die
                temperature.
                uwb::Qm33120::init()を丸ごとやり直す
                （UWB_TWR_DIAG_REINIT_FAILSと同じ経路。main.cppの
                diagReinit()参照）。PLL/PGF/ADCのキャリブレーションが
                まとめて走る。

    endchoice

    config UWB_TWR_DIAG_RECAL_SEC
        int "Diagnostic: seconds after start to run the re-calibration (UWB_TWR_DIAG_RECAL_KIND)"
        range 5 600
        default 40
        help
            How long after boot (esp_timer_get_time()) the TAG performs the
            UWB_TWR_DIAG_RECAL_KIND calibration once (ignored when
            UWB_TWR_DIAG_RECAL_KIND is NONE). Long enough to collect a
            "before" success-rate sample - a few hundred ranging attempts at
            the default 200ms poll interval - before it fires.
            起動（esp_timer_get_time()）から何秒後に、TAGが
            UWB_TWR_DIAG_RECAL_KINDのキャリブレーションを1回だけ実行するか
            （UWB_TWR_DIAG_RECAL_KINDがNONEのときは無視される）。発火前に
            「前」側の成功率サンプル（既定200ms間隔で数百回分）を集められる
            だけの長さにしてある。

    choice UWB_TIMING_PROFILE
        prompt "TWR timing preset"
        default UWB_TIMING_PROFILE_BOTH_IRQ
        help
            Selects the delay-parameter preset (role x IRQ-availability)
            fixed in docs/TIMING_PRESETS.md (response delay, RX timeout,
            etc).

            **TAG and ANCHOR must use the same preset.** A one-sided change
            breaks ranging - and the only symptom is "no distance", with the
            log alone unable to tell which side is wrong. To catch this, the
            actually-applied version number and profile are carried in the
            Poll/Response frames so the receiving side can compare against
            its own and warn on a mismatch (ranging still proceeds -
            docs/TIMING_PRESETS.md SS3).

            This setting is never changed automatically. For example, if
            AnchorIrq is selected but pin_irq is unwired, the wait falls
            back to polling while the delay values themselves stay
            unchanged; only a boot-time warning is logged
            (docs/TIMING_PRESETS.md SS4(b)).

        config UWB_TIMING_PROFILE_POLLING_BOTH
            bool "Polling on both sides (~31 Hz, identical to the current default)"

        config UWB_TIMING_PROFILE_ANCHOR_IRQ
            bool "IRQ on the anchor only (~59 Hz, standard configuration)"

        config UWB_TIMING_PROFILE_BOTH_IRQ
            bool "IRQ on both sides (~90 Hz, when the tag can be wired separately)"

    endchoice

    config UWB_ENABLE_IRQ
        bool "Use IRQ as a wakeup signal (falls back to polling automatically if unwired)"
        default y
        help
            Use the IRQ (interrupt request) line only as a "wakeup signal"
            for the receive-wait loops. Status-register decoding, frame
            matching, and error handling always go through the same
            polling-derived code path regardless of whether IRQ is enabled
            (dwt_setcallbacks()/dwt_isr() are intentionally not used - see
            docs/IRQ_POLICY.md).

            Anchor-role boards (AtomS3, pin_irq wired) are the primary
            beneficiary; TAG-role boards on StampFly have no pin_irq wired
            at all and always fall back to polling regardless of this
            setting. The default is y: the active-high polarity is backed
            by the datasheet and was verified on real hardware (probe L5
            IRQ self-test, 2026-08-29; ranging with IRQ enabled, 2026-08-30).

            Even when enabled, an unwired pin_irq or a failed ISR
            registration falls back to polling automatically
            (uwb::Qm33120::irqActive() reports whether IRQ actually ended
            up active; this is also logged at boot). The polling path is
            always kept as a first-class implementation, not a degraded
            fallback.

endmenu
